From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: zed-patches <zed-patches@localhost>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 19:00:00 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] agent_servers: Zeo's running MCP servers reach Claude Agent
 (Plus) over ACP
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Zeo proposal §6.69 step 3 (ask 94), built with §6.13 as one story. Zed sends
every enabled context server to an external agent in session/new as its
command line (stdio) or URL (http), and the agent starts its own copy. Zeo
already runs one copy per open project, so on 2026-11-22 the one extension
server the operator uses ran as 18 processes, about 1.7 GB, each with its
API key in argv (docs/assets/zeo-asks-2026-11-22/C-mcp-skills.md, C1). A
jailed agent could not start an extension server at all: its binary lives
under ~/.local/share/zeo, which the jail hides (0146 leaves such servers out).

MCP-over-ACP carries the server over the agent's own ACP connection instead.
Claude Agent (Plus) advertises mcpCapabilities.acp since its mcp-over-acp
release and turns each McpServer::Acp { name, serverId } into an in-process
SDK server whose calls come back to Zeo as mcp/message (ACP 5.4.0, schema
1.19, MCP 2026-07-28 -- the stateless binding, no initialize).

Declaring (v1, the path Plus takes): on session/new, load, resume and fork,
every entry naming a context server that is Running or Starting becomes an
acp declaration, when the agent advertised mcpCapabilities.acp and
agent.mcp_servers_over_acp is on (default true, assets/settings/default.json).
Gated on the capability, as every _claude/* feature in the series is gated on
what the agent says: only Plus advertises it, and the native Zed agent never
goes through AcpConnection. A stopped server, a remote project and an agent
without the capability keep today's stdio/http entries. The serverId is
zeo-<project entity id>-<name>: the same on every request of one connection,
because Plus folds the server list into its session fingerprint and a fresh
id would tear the session down on every reload.

Serving (acp/mcp_over_acp.rs, acp/mcp_over_acp_forward.rs): a tenth v1
request handler, on the foreground like the other nine.
- server/discover is answered from the handshake Zeo did when it started the
  server: supportedVersions ["2026-07-28"], capabilities, serverInfo and
  instructions (0148). Plus answers the CLI's initialize from it.
- ping is answered; every other method is forwarded verbatim to the running
  server through 0148's request_raw, with the binding's per-request
  io.modelcontextprotocol/* _meta taken off (the stateful server knows none
  of it). The result and an inner MCP error go back as they came.
- progress: a request carrying _meta.progressToken is sent with a token
  unique to Zeo (two agents may forward the same token to one shared server)
  and the server's notifications/progress come back as mcp/message
  notifications under the agent's own token, until the request ends.
- cancellation: the agent's $/cancel_request (what Plus's McpOverAcpCaller
  sends on abort) sends notifications/cancelled to the server and answers
  -32800.
- an undeclared serverId is -33001 (serverUnavailable), a backend failure
  -33002, a duplicate active (serverId, requestId) -32602, as the binding
  defines them; a server still starting is waited for, up to 30 s.
- one log line per request (server, serverId, method, outcome, code, ms),
  debug on success, warn on failure; never params or results.

The jail hook: McpProxyPolicy, which servers one connection may reach through
the proxy (AcpConnection::mcp_proxy_policy, All here). A proxied server runs on
the host, outside any jail, so the jail group narrows it (0150).

Not in this patch: change notifications (list_changed) and server-to-client
requests, as on Plus's side; the v2 transport (acp-beta flag only, which Plus
does not use); remote projects.

Tests mcp_over_acp_tests (new; harness mcp_over_acp_harness: a scripted ACP
agent against the real AcpConnection and handler set, a ScriptedTransport
context server behind it):
a running server is declared as acp with no command line; an agent without
the capability and the setting off keep the command; the serverId is the
same for every session; discover answers from the server's handshake;
tools/call round-trips a result and an inner error, without the binding's
_meta reaching the server; progress reaches the agent under its own token;
a cancel tells the server and answers -32800; an undeclared id is -33001; a
policy proxies only the servers it names.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
